<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bobi Wine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1982</span> · Also known as Robert Kyagulanyi, Robert Kyagulanyi Ssentamu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bobi Wine, the stage name of Robert Kyagulanyi Ssentamu, is a Ugandan musician and politician. Elected to parliament in 2017, he led the People Power movement and then the National Unity Platform in opposition to President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoweri-museveni">Yoweri Museveni</a>, and was the main challenger in the presidential election of January 2021, which he lost amid violence against his supporters and allegations of fraud.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bobi-wine.jpg" alt="Bobi Wine" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: VoA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bobi_Wine_2024.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
